<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Believers</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Old Believers are Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christians who rejected the liturgical reforms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patriarch-nikon">Patriarch Nikon</a> in the 1650s and 1660s. Persecuted by church and state, many fled to the frontiers, and they were numerous among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> hosts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-river">Yaik</a> and Terek and among settlers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>. Their communities survive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and abroad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-believers.jpg" alt="Old Believers" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Voice of America · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Believers_in_Alaska_7D58CCE1-1C6F-4882-923D-E27A39EBCFC1_w1023_n_r1_st.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1650s the liturgical reforms of Patriarch Nikon split the church: the <b>Old Believers</b> who rejected them were condemned in 1666–1667, and their leader Avvakum was burned in 1682.</blockquote><a href="/empire/tsardom-of-russia">Tsardom of Russia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Old Russian church architecture, with its many domes and wooden forms, drew on pre-Christian building, and some scholars find early Slavic ideas among the <b>Old Believers</b> who split from the church after Patriarch Nikon’s reform of 1656.</blockquote><a href="/religion/slavic-paganism">Slavic paganism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>Many Cossacks of the Ural and the Terek were <b>Old Believers</b>.</blockquote><a href="/societies/russian-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Russian Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>They clashed repeatedly with the Nekrasov Cossacks, Russian <b>Old Believers</b> settled nearby, over fishing grounds and Ottoman favour.</blockquote><a href="/state/danube-sich">Danube Sich</a></li><li><blockquote>The Mughan steppe and Lankaran area had many Russian settler villages, including Molokans and <b>Old Believers</b>, established in the 19th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/provisional-military-dictatorship-of-mughan">Provisional Military Dictatorship of Mughan</a></li></ul></section>
